Subject: [PATCH 5/8] ps_dec: parametric stereo's decorrelator and mixing four subbands (or bands) at a time

VibeSDR patch for FAAD2 2.11.3 (the plain build VibeServer links for DAB+ audio, libfaad_dab.a). GPL-2.0-or-later,
as FAAD2. Written for VibeSDR, 2026-10-26; applied by vibeserver/linux/build-deps.sh and vibeserver/mac/build-deps.sh
in the order of faad2-patches/series. Measured on real off-air DAB+ unit logs (HE-AAC v2, 21 logs, 1909 s):
output against stock FAAD2 2.11.3 built with its own flags — see each header for the figures.

Parametric stereo's decorrelator runs every QMF subband up to nr_allpass_bands through a three-link fractional all-pass
chain, one time slot after another. Every subband sees the same delay-index sequence (each starts from saved_delay /
delay_buf_index_ser), so four adjacent subbands run as four lanes sharing their indices; each lane keeps its own
phasors, decay slope and transient ratio (its own parameter band). The arithmetic per lane is the stock loop's; the
subbands done here are skipped by the stock loop, which still does the rest (the hybrid bands and any remainder of
fewer than four). Also four at a time: the plain 14-slot delay above nr_allpass_bands (lanes sharing the delay's length
and position), a QMF group's energy per time slot (summed in lanes, then added: a different float addition order, within
rounding), the transient ratio per parameter band (each band's recursion as stock; its divide a true divide on SSE2 and
AArch64, a twice-refined reciprocal on ARMv7, ~2 ulp), and the mixing of a group's subbands with the group's H.

